{"Title":"An Act providing for equal access to certain roadways under the jurisdiction of the department of conservation and recreation","BillNumber":"S2895","DocketNumber":null,"GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"S30","Name":"Senate Committee on Ways and Means","Type":2,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/S30","ResponseDate":"2024-07-25T11:12:52.997"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"N_C0","Name":"Nick Collins","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/N_C0","ResponseDate":"2023-10-06T11:34:44.9766667"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/S2895/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"Senate, July 29, 2024 -- The committee on Senate Ways and Means, to whom was referred the Senate Bill relative to equal access on DCR roadways (Senate, No. 2557),- reports, recommending that the same ought to pass with an amendment entitled \"An Act providing for equal access to certain roadways under the jurisdiction of the department of conservation and recreation\"  (Senate, No. 2894).","DocumentText":"\tSection 1 of chapter 164 of the acts of 2022 is hereby amended by inserting after the first sentence the following sentence:- Any such easement shall grant the same rights of access for the benefit of all other properties on the Columbia Point peninsula located between William T. Morrissey Boulevard, William J. Day Boulevard and Dorchester Bay.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[],"Amendments":[]}